      'Curls along the floor of the temporal horn: <b>head</b> (with digitations), <b>body</b>, <b>tail</b>. Subfields in section: dentate gyrus, CA1–CA4, subiculum, with entorhinal and perirhinal cortex as the cortical gateway.',
      '<b>Trisynaptic circuit:</b> entorhinal layer II → (perforant path) → dentate granule cells → (mossy fibres) → CA3 → (Schaffer collaterals) → CA1 → subiculum → entorhinal layer V. A parallel direct path runs EC layer III → CA1.',
      'Long-axis specialisation: anterior (ventral) hippocampus is connected with amygdala and hypothalamus (emotion, stress, gist), posterior (dorsal) with retrosplenial and parietal cortex (fine spatial detail).'
