      { dir: 'Efferent', txt: '<b>Direct:</b> D1 MSN → GPi/SNr (inhibition) → thalamic disinhibition → cortex facilitation. <b>Indirect:</b> D2 MSN → GPe → STN → GPi/SNr → thalamic inhibition. <b>Hyperdirect:</b> cortex → STN, bypassing striatum, for rapid stopping.' },
      { dir: 'Loop', txt: 'Five parallel CSTC loops (Alexander, DeLong & Strick, 1986). Their functional segregation means a small striatal lesion can produce a purely cognitive or purely affective syndrome with no motor sign at all.' }
